  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7ed8d592803d6492b8f1f0ac1555a1ea, type: 3}
  m_Name: UserData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: InsightsSamples.Common::InsightsSamples.Common.SampleInfo
  id: 10-user-data
  number: 10
  title: User data
  series: Context & identity
  icon: id-card
  scenario: Employee badge at a shared headset
  realWorld: "A cart of shared headsets serves a whole shift. Each employee taps their badge first, so their sessions and results belong to them by employee ID, not to whichever headset they picked up."
  teaches: SetUserData, GetUserData, GetUserId
  sceneName: UserData
  appWidePrefab: {fileID: 0}
  whatThisShows: Identify the learner with SetUserData, and read back what Insights
    knows with GetUserData and GetUserId. Identity lives in userData, never in event
    metadata.
  tryThis:
  - Tap Sam's badge (E-1042) to set the user data, then click Check user data.
  - 'Tap the visitor badge: no user data is set.'
  - SetUserData needs a signed-in session. Sign in (sample 01) to see it sync.
  watchFor:
  - SetUserData makes no record. Once the SDK has signed in again, an OnUserDataSyncCompleted
    row (System filter).
  - 'Check user data shows GetUserId() and GetUserData(): null until signed in.'
  lessonScript: UserDataSample.cs
  lessonScriptLine: 26
  dashboardNotes:
  - methodPrefix: OnUserDataSync
    note: 'Learner identity: who each session''s records belong to'
  expectedOnPass: []
  expectedOnFail: []
